//! atoms — the smallest Zeus pieces: a single glyph, hairline, label, badge,
//! avatar, or meter. They compose nothing but `zeusbase` (Component, the props
//! structs, the tokens, signals), so every tier above can build on them.
//!
//! Tier order is load order. `zeus` imports atoms, then molecules, then
//! organisms, and each tier imports the one below it. C struct typedefs are
//! emitted per module in load order, so a struct used as a field must live in a
//! tier at or below its user.
//!
//! The widget moves land here next: Icon, Pip, Row/RowWrap/Column/Grow,
//! Separator/Divider, the type-scale labels (Overline, Display, Heading, Title,
//! Body, Note, SectionHeader, SectionTitle), Kbd, Chip, Badge/BadgeCount,
//! Progress, Meter, Surface, Avatar/AvatarGroup, Sparkline, Stat/StatCount,
//! Skeleton, Spinner, and Empty.

import "std:structs"
import "std:enums"
import "std:zeusbase"
import "std:zeus_constants"
